# drizzle/meta is deliberately COMMITTED. _journal.json is what tells the migrator
# which migrations exist, and the snapshots are what drizzle-kit diffs to generate
# the next one. Ignoring them meant a clean checkout could not migrate at all: the
# CLI uploads the working directory using its own ignore list rather than this file,
# so a laptop's untracked journal shipped with every deploy and hid the gap. It
# surfaced the moment CI built from git.

# Real bank statements contain private financial data — never commit them.
# (Keep your sample locally; it's just the import format reference.)
